From 37c9ffa527014e6823d517116248d7a0676a8a07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CLAUDE <355856132+HoTT-stuff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:28:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add multinomial and Dirichlet-multinomial differential
 abundance through MGLM

Two new values of analysis.differential.method, as ruled on issue #22: MN/DM
regression comes in through MGLM via RCall, with MGLM pinned in renv.lock.

- multinomial and dirichlet_multinomial fit one MGLM::MGLMreg.fit model of the
  composition of the taxa passing min_prevalence, conditioned on each sample's
  read total (dist "MN" or "DM"). Every estimate is the change in a taxon's log
  ratio to a reference taxon, with a Wald z-test and BH adjustment over the
  fitted taxa. For DM the contrast is the difference of two group
  coefficients, and its standard error takes their covariance from the
  inverse observed information.
- analysis.differential.mn_reference_taxon names the reference; empty uses
  the fitted taxon with the most reads. Its row has status "reference".
- A taxon with no reads in every sample of one group is failed and left out
  of the composition (complete separation). DM needs 2 samples per group. At
  most 1000 taxa enter one fit.
- A fit that errors, reaches MGLM's iteration cap, warns that it did not
  converge or is not a maximum, or whose information is not positive
  definite fails every taxon with that reason. MGLM's options(warn = -1) is
  restored whatever happens.
- When a DM group shows no overdispersion, its concentration has no finite
  estimate. The rows are marked boundary and keep their statistics, since a
  log-ratio contrast does not depend on that concentration; or MGLM's own
  refusal is kept and names the flat group. Only when both groups are flat
  are the estimates the multinomial's, and only then is multinomial
  suggested.
- MGLMUnavailable is a 503 at the route; MGLM is added to the installer, the
  runtime package list and the CI package checks.
- Tests: the multinomial against its closed form (pooled log ratios, SE from
  reciprocal pooled counts), the Dirichlet-multinomial against stats::optim
  on an independently written likelihood with stats::optimHess, the boundary
  with one group and with both groups flat, refusals, separation, the 503
  path and the route.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0136P7ZoFbrtmpRbKPqk25ok
